  "source_roles": {
    "corpus": "Pang’s PAL carry and return question, RPL square scale, APCI same-input test, and earlier two-clock calculation motivated the reversible rescaling.",
    "mathematical_inputs": [
      "The actual project edge and the finite lower bound at a zeta zero from the signed-area paper.",
      "Stone gives the nonlattice local limit mechanism. The paper derives the uniform two-clock calculation and treats the varying tilt directly.",
      "Theorem 2.2, equations (21) and (23) of Lee and Leong (arXiv:2208.06141v5) supplies unconditional Mertens estimates. The paper transports those estimates to its positive interval. The live two-row paper now links to the exact version and equation."
    ],
    "links": [
      "https://digicoll.lib.berkeley.edu/record/113081/files/math_s5_v2_p2_article-15.pdf",
      "https://arxiv.org/html/2208.06141v5#S2.SS2"
    ]
  },
  "formal_result": "SignCheckpoints implies stock Mathlib RiemannHypothesis. For each positive integer q and starting index B the premise supplies a later head 2^N, a positive pass count k with q*k <= N, and nonnegative signs for all 2^(N+1) explicit rational samples. Interpolation, area transport and the inverse are derived. The premise remains open.",
