  "paper_results": [
    "For sufficiently large k all rows with 1/2 < x <= 12^k exp(a k^(5/7)/(log(2+k))^(1/7)) are strictly positive for some absolute a > 0. The reading is zero through 1/2.",
    "Under RH every fixed number of doublings per pass is attained uniformly throughout the interval for all sufficiently large k. The cofinal all-rates criterion is equivalent to RH on paper.",
    "If a fixed rate can be attained at arbitrarily late heads, rate 19 would exclude zeros of real part at least 151/152, rate 23 at least 171/184, and rate 56 at least 3/4.",
    "For each fixed k, a zero of real part beta > 1/2 would force at least c(rho,k) H^(2 beta - 1) negative half-rows at every sufficiently large integer head. Subpower counts of exceptions suffice along sublinear-pass heads."
  ],
